 falls from 12-team field in 4th CFP rankings; Horns, Vols leap Bama","description":"Defending champ Indiana fell six spots to No. 14, while Alabama was leaped by Texas and Tennessee and fell out of the top five in the latest CFP rankings Tuesday night.","published":"2026-11-25T07:42:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588082/indiana-top-12-cfp-rankings-texas-tennessee-leap-alabama","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's fourth top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's fourth set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T02:02:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584328/cfp-2026-fourth-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5132218/kameryn-crawford","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kameryn_Crawford"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Kameryn Crawford","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kameryn_Crawford","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Kameryn Crawford is an American college football defensive end for the USC Trojans.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Crawford attended Booker T. Washington High School in Atlanta. As a senior in 2023, he was the Region 6-AA Co-Defensive Player of the Year. Crawford was selected to play in the 2024 Under Armour All-American Game. He committed to the University of Southern California (USC) to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at USC in 2024, Crawford played in eight games with four starts and had 19 tackles. He returned to USC in 2025 and earned more playing time. During the season, he changed his name from Kameryn Fountain to Kameryn Crawford."}]}}